WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.418
- You see I got the shirt
tucked in, right?

00:00:01.418 --> 00:00:02.836
- That don't mean nothing to me.
- You know what that means?

00:00:02.836 --> 00:00:04.045
- No, I don't know what it means.

00:00:04.045 --> 00:00:05.880
- I got this shirt
tucked in, right?
- What's that mean?

00:00:05.880 --> 00:00:07.132
- That means you learned how
to put your shirt in your pants.

00:00:07.132 --> 00:00:08.508
- Listen, when you go on a job

00:00:08.508 --> 00:00:09.634
don't you go
with your shirt tucked in?

00:00:09.634 --> 00:00:11.636
Cuz you mean business, right?

00:00:14.097 --> 00:00:16.057
Hello.
I am Chad Johnson.

00:00:16.057 --> 00:00:18.059
I am here with my good friend

00:00:18.059 --> 00:00:21.438
and Hall of Fame
receiver Terrell Owens

00:00:21.438 --> 00:00:25.191
and up-and-coming
draft prospect

00:00:25.191 --> 00:00:30.113
one of the best receivers
in the nation, Riley Ridley.

00:00:30.113 --> 00:00:34.909
- Riley Ridley stepping up!
- Touchdown, Riley Ridley.

00:00:34.909 --> 00:00:37.620
- Touchdown, Georgia!

00:00:37.620 --> 00:00:40.999
- What do you feel like your
best asset is as a receiver?

00:00:40.999 --> 00:00:42.917
- Right now, I'm physical.
- OK.

00:00:42.917 --> 00:00:44.878
- I'm physical, more physical
than any receiver

00:00:44.878 --> 00:00:45.962
going into the draft.

00:00:45.962 --> 00:00:47.922
I'm more physical than any DB.

00:00:47.922 --> 00:00:50.008
- So that's something that
you don't have to work on.

00:00:50.008 --> 00:00:53.762
So now, you gotta worry about—
work on the finesse part of the game.

00:00:53.762 --> 00:00:56.973
- So you got T: muscle.
- Right.
- Physical.

00:00:56.973 --> 00:00:59.476
- Physical, get through you,
and then you have my skill set

00:00:59.476 --> 00:01:01.728
where it's completely opposite.

00:01:01.728 --> 00:01:03.480
"Don't touch me."

00:01:03.480 --> 00:01:06.232
How I like to do it—like,
I like to get jiggy at the line.

00:01:06.232 --> 00:01:07.650
Man, let's ride with it.

00:01:07.650 --> 00:01:09.736
Oh, 'scuse me.
And I need all this space.

00:01:09.736 --> 00:01:11.780
- My coach said—
he said this to me

00:01:11.780 --> 00:01:13.740
because he knew
I liked basketball.

00:01:13.740 --> 00:01:15.909
- Right.
- And this is what clicked for me.

00:01:15.909 --> 00:01:18.745
He said you have to treat
the defensive back

00:01:18.745 --> 00:01:20.497
like you're playin' one-on-one.

00:01:20.497 --> 00:01:22.415
If you playin' one-on-one
and you tryin' to get by me

00:01:22.415 --> 00:01:24.042
what are you gonna do?

00:01:24.042 --> 00:01:25.168
- I'm gonna make some moves.
- You gotta make me move.

00:01:25.168 --> 00:01:26.628
- Right.

00:01:26.628 --> 00:01:28.213
- Same thing with every route,
pretty much

00:01:28.213 --> 00:01:30.381
cuz I'm tryin'
to score a bucket.

00:01:30.381 --> 00:01:32.634
- That's what I'm tryin' to get at.
I'm here.

00:01:32.634 --> 00:01:33.927
I'm gonna give you two steps

00:01:33.927 --> 00:01:35.136
and then I'm gettin'
right into this.

00:01:35.136 --> 00:01:36.888
- OK, show me.
- So I'm here, and I'm gone.

00:01:36.888 --> 00:01:38.473
- OK.

00:01:38.473 --> 00:01:40.725
Initially when you came off
the ball, boom-boom

00:01:40.725 --> 00:01:42.477
you kinda
got wide a little bit.

00:01:42.477 --> 00:01:44.312
Try to stay a little—

00:01:44.312 --> 00:01:46.106
Try to engage them a little bit
more, you know what I mean?
- Absolutely, mhmm.

00:01:46.106 --> 00:01:47.690
- So I like what you did.

00:01:47.690 --> 00:01:50.151
Boom-boom-boom, here,
then kinda get into him.

00:01:50.151 --> 00:01:51.778
Invite him.
Invite him.

00:01:51.778 --> 00:01:55.240
And when you here, you wanna
show that acceleration

00:01:55.240 --> 00:01:57.575
like you about to go deep.
- Deep.
- Then you stop.

00:01:57.575 --> 00:02:00.120
My problem was, when I used
to get it going in my breaks

00:02:00.120 --> 00:02:04.082
I used to—yeah, I used to have
these flappers right here.

00:02:04.082 --> 00:02:05.667
Then my coach told me

00:02:05.667 --> 00:02:07.752
I had to be a drummer boy,
you know what I mean?

00:02:07.752 --> 00:02:09.003
Be a drummer boy.

00:02:09.003 --> 00:02:10.755
Then when I did, when I did it here

00:02:10.755 --> 00:02:13.258
transition, it's in
and out of my breaks quick.

00:02:13.258 --> 00:02:14.676
- Right.

00:02:14.676 --> 00:02:15.885
- We're trying to get you
to become a salesman

00:02:15.885 --> 00:02:17.470
before you actually a salesman.

00:02:17.470 --> 00:02:22.308
I do a dig route based off
a, off a comeback stance.

00:02:22.308 --> 00:02:24.811
I call it send the dude
to the Gatorade.

00:02:24.811 --> 00:02:26.479
I'm gonna send him
to the Gatorade.

00:02:26.479 --> 00:02:28.982
So, just say—
come here, come in here.

00:02:28.982 --> 00:02:30.817
Just say the ball is in there.

00:02:30.817 --> 00:02:32.902
- Right.
- The ball is in there.

00:02:32.902 --> 00:02:34.821
And I got a dig route.

00:02:34.821 --> 00:02:36.489
So this is what I'm gonna do.

00:02:36.489 --> 00:02:39.242
Boom, boom,
I'm gonna get him right here.

00:02:39.242 --> 00:02:43.037
Aha.
I—oooh.

00:02:43.037 --> 00:02:44.455
I'mma send him
to the Gatorade.

00:02:44.455 --> 00:02:47.292
- No doubt.
- All this right here is open.

00:02:47.292 --> 00:02:50.378
Cuz as soon as you nod
that way, he gone.

00:02:50.378 --> 00:02:54.841
- And very seldom on deep balls
do you just blow by a dude.

00:02:54.841 --> 00:02:56.759
That ain't happenin'.
- Yeah.

00:02:56.759 --> 00:02:58.219
- That ain't happenin'

00:02:58.219 --> 00:02:59.262
unless you just beat
somebody off the line.

00:02:59.262 --> 00:03:00.930
You just gas him.
- Yeah, exactly.

00:03:00.930 --> 00:03:03.933
- I mean, you got to be
goddamn Tyreek Hill or some—

00:03:03.933 --> 00:03:06.519
That's a different ballgame.
- Randy is one of those guys.

00:03:06.519 --> 00:03:07.979
- Randy.
- There's a few guys.

00:03:07.979 --> 00:03:09.522
- Yeah, Randy, you see
the mailbox like—

00:03:09.522 --> 00:03:12.442
- When he throw that hand up—
- It's really over.

00:03:12.442 --> 00:03:14.152
- Not, not everybody is like that.

00:03:14.152 --> 00:03:15.653
He's freakish.

00:03:15.653 --> 00:03:17.697
Just freakishly fast,
you know what I mean

00:03:17.697 --> 00:03:19.407
to the point that he start
coming off the line

00:03:19.407 --> 00:03:22.368
and he already
sticking his hands up.

00:03:22.368 --> 00:03:24.037
Right,
he's sticking his hands up.

00:03:24.037 --> 00:03:26.164
- DB five yards away,
he gonna throw his hand up.

00:03:26.164 --> 00:03:28.124
It's a bunch of receivers
in the NFL.

00:03:28.124 --> 00:03:29.417
There's 32 teams.

00:03:29.417 --> 00:03:31.127
There's a No. 1
on every team.
- Right.

00:03:31.127 --> 00:03:32.712
- What's the difference in each
No. 1

00:03:32.712 --> 00:03:34.505
and the rest of the receivers
on the team?

00:03:34.505 --> 00:03:36.966
It's something about that dude
that makes him special.

00:03:36.966 --> 00:03:38.927
It's something about Odell
that makes him different

00:03:38.927 --> 00:03:40.553
than the rest of the Giants receivers.
- Right.

00:03:40.553 --> 00:03:42.764
There's something about AB
that makes him special.

00:03:42.764 --> 00:03:44.849
Something about Julio.

00:03:44.849 --> 00:03:47.185
You got to go out wherever you go,
and when you get there

00:03:47.185 --> 00:03:49.270
there gotta be something
about f--king Ridley

00:03:49.270 --> 00:03:51.272
that makes him special.
- Exactly.

00:03:51.272 --> 00:03:53.024
- That separates him
from everybody else.

00:03:53.024 --> 00:03:54.567
- No doubt.
- Whether it's the way you work

00:03:54.567 --> 00:03:56.069
whether it's your hands,
whether it's your feet

00:03:56.069 --> 00:03:57.528
whether it's your routes,
whether it's you

00:03:57.528 --> 00:04:01.282
being consistent,
gotta be something. One!

00:04:01.282 --> 00:04:02.909
Ain't gotta be
a bunch of things.

00:04:02.909 --> 00:04:05.161
It's one thing about Floyd
that makes him great.

00:04:05.161 --> 00:04:07.080
There's a f--kin'
million boxers!

00:04:07.080 --> 00:04:09.415
- Yeah.
- You not gonna hit me.

00:04:09.415 --> 00:04:11.209
I'mma hit you whenever I want.

00:04:11.209 --> 00:04:13.419
So as a receiver, you find
whatever that niche about you

00:04:13.419 --> 00:04:16.297
that makes you special,
it's a wrap.

00:04:16.297 --> 00:04:19.342
- I got a brother in the NFL,
but to be able to go

00:04:19.342 --> 00:04:20.969
through this on your own,
you know what I'm sayin'

00:04:20.969 --> 00:04:23.221
and have great people around you

00:04:23.221 --> 00:04:24.973
and willing to help you,
it's amazing.

00:04:24.973 --> 00:04:26.307
- And Calvin Ridley,
if you see this

00:04:26.307 --> 00:04:32.063
I will lock you up, period.
- [Laughing]
- Period.

00:04:32.063 --> 00:04:35.400
- No, you ain't finna to lock
nobody up, dawg.

00:04:35.400 --> 00:04:37.235
Nobody.
- Check my resume.

